    <!-- REMOVED 2026-09-15 (generation 9): model MaleVisitorOnPhone, a human
         figure at (2, 2) with a mesh collision and semantic label 8. The N=2
         spawn points sit 2.83 m and 2.24 m from it, and at N=4 three of the
         four are within 2.83 m, all inside the 0.40-1.00 m height band
         simple_nav_3d counts obstacles in. So every run in every arm began by
         driving around a mannequin. It is scene furniture from another world's
         demo; nothing in the experiment reads label 8, and it had already cost
         the target list a candidate (targets_flatforest.yaml, the target file
         these campaigns actually load, skips "Oak tree_19" partly because this
         model stands 0.120 m from that trunk, measured). The other reason to
         skip that tree, that its vantage ring would sit on the spawn point, is
         independent and still holds, so the target list is unchanged.
